PsyZ patch for the port. Written by this project; applies to PsyZ commit
4c68cab400cba341be3d2066993fcdf778301acf (port/external/psyz at its pin).
Applied by port/tools/psyzbuild.py to a copy of PsyZ, never to the submodule.

License: the PsyZ files this patch changes are under the
Mozilla Public License 2.0 by PsyZ's LICENSE file at that commit. The context
lines that the hunks below quote stay under that license, and this
change to them is offered under the same one: this Source Code Form is
subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0. A copy of it is
at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.

What it fixes: in GPU_Enqueue (psyz/src/psyz/libgpu.c), the path for hosts
whose unsigned long is 4 bytes draws the packets into PsyZ's vertex batch
but flushes the batch only when compiled for the browser (__EMSCRIPTEN__).
On a 32-bit native build nothing that a program draws reaches the picture
until something else flushes, and the readback of a drawn primitive shows
the clear colour only. In one run on one machine on 2026-10-09, PsyZ's own
picture tests built for i686 failed 25 of 37 in the gpu area and passed 37
of 37 with the flush made unconditional; no command of this repository
repeats that run. The 64-bit path does flush (through Psyz_GpuExeque), so
only the 32-bit path needs this.

At PsyZ commit 6d01339aadf16c5c9d6e44f44c0d66514752e472 the function
Psyz_GpuExeque also flushes the batch on 32-bit targets (PsyZ's change #178),
which covers the drop at the next DrawSync, LoadImage or StoreImage. On
2026-10-10 the port's picture test passed with this patch and without it, so
it does not show the patch to be needed there; the patch is kept.


Batched uploads: with Psyz_Sfa2SetBatchedUploads(1) (the port's setting fast_loads) the LoadImage calls that go into one command buffer share the
upload transfer buffer, one after the other, instead of cycling it for every call. A screen change makes the game call LoadImage over a thousand
times; each cycle made the driver allocate a new buffer of the whole size, and those calls took 160 to 600 ms. With it off nothing changes.

Output volume: Psyz_Sfa2SetVolume(gain) sets the gain of the one SDL audio stream that PsyZ opens (SDL_SetAudioStreamGain), and
Psyz_AudioInit applies the stored gain before it starts the stream, so a call before the device opens also counts. The port's
--volume PERCENT calls it. Nothing else of the audio path changes.

Optional graphics: the SDL_GPU backend consumes an explicit port marker for
super/life pixel-grid tiles and selected six-row health fills. It also exposes
an opt-in 384x224/4:3 canvas. With
both flags disabled, normal texture sampling and presentation remain unchanged.
The project-authored shared policy header is copied by psyzbuild.py. No shader
or global UV correction is changed. The port selects only its known HUD tiles.

